course: dictionary
lesson: 6702
title: Odd, and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word odd has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one to use. In «The rules that seem odd have good reasons», odd means strange or unusual, the way something looks at first.
explain: Look at «devyanOsto means ninety; it is an odd one, not built as "nine" plus "-ty".» Here odd means unusual, because the word does not follow the usual pattern. Nobody is talking about numbers.
explain: In maths, odd means a number that cannot be split into two equal whole groups, like 1, 3, 5 or 7. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence, then try it. Does «seven is an odd number» make sense? Yes, so that meaning fits.
explain: Odd can also mean a few, now and then, as in «odd jobs» or «the odd sweet». Ben does odd jobs for his neighbour, so he does a few small jobs now and then.
fact: Odd has several meanings, so check the words around it before you choose one.
fact: An odd number cannot be split into two equal whole groups, like 1, 3, 5 or 7.
fact: An odd sock is one sock without its pair, and an odd one out is the one that does not belong.
fact: Odd can mean strange or unusual, as in «that's odd» or «strange hands and odd backgrounds» in AI pictures.
fact: The comparison forms are odd, odder, oddest.
exercise: «Languages keep changing, borrowing and playing, so the best language skill is curiosity: notice odd words, ask what they mean.» In this sentence, what does odd mean? | *Strange or unusual, so worth noticing | Very wet | A number you cannot split in two equal groups | Not part of a pair
exercise: Which of these numbers is odd? | 10 | 6 | *9 | 4
exercise: «AI can make pictures with strange hands, blurry writing and odd backgrounds.» What does odd suggest here? | A number that is split | Heavy | Part of a pair | *Strange or unusual, not what you would expect
test: «The rules that seem odd have good reasons: no food beforehand so nothing can come up into the lungs.» What does odd mean here? | A number you cannot split in two | Very tasty | Not part of a pair | *Strange or unusual at first sight
test: «Ben does odd jobs for his neighbour.» What does odd mean here? | *A few, now and then | Not in a pair | Equal in two groups | Strange and rude
exam: Which sentence uses odd to mean a number that cannot be split into two equal groups? | Mia has an odd sock. | That is odd behaviour. | *Seven is an odd number. | I ate the odd sweet.
